  "query_preview": "..\nToday through Friday AM: As yesterday's weather system has exited\nthe region, higher pressure has filled in behind, letting the \narea dry out from the precipitation received yesterday. \nSynoptically speaking, ridging aloft with NW flow currently then \nquickly transitioning to troughing by Friday. Today, expect dry \nconditions. The Lake Wind Advisory expired at 2 AM today. No \nsignificant impacts expected during this period. \n\nFriday PM through Tuesday: Large scale upper-level troughing \ncontinues across the western US the remainder of the week. The \nnext system will bring another shot of colder air from the north \nthis weekend. A cut-off low is forecast to eject into the main \nflow which will bring a weather system to the region Friday \nmorning and into Saturday. This will bring the next isolated \nchance for snow. Isolated chances of snow across the area but the \nmain impact will be the below normal temperatures. Snow chances \nappear on the western side of our higher elevation areas of our \nCWA, as early as 12 PM Friday and as late as 6 PM Friday. Expect \nonset of flurries for lower elevation areas sometime between \nFriday afternoon into Saturday morning. Wind chills this weekend \nare forecast to be in the teens during the AM hours and likely \ndipping in the upper-single digits. A frontal passage Friday \nnight/Saturday morning may bring speeds back up high enough to \nwarrant a Lake Wind Advisory that morning. An update \ntonight/tomorrow will be provided once model guidance narrows down\ntiming/intensity of wind speeds. All in all, trace amounts \nexpected in lower elevations. Impacts during this period remain \nminimal.\n\nTuesday night onward: A weak ridge to quasi-zonal flow pattern\nwill set in leading the region back to warmer near normal temps \nwith highs in the 30s and 40s. Models begin to disagree Tuesday, \nleading to a higher uncertainty in temperatures and heights \nTuesday night onward. \n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\n- Deviations today include increasing PoPs by blending in the \n  Euro and GFS. No further changes to NBM were made. \n\n- Moderate confidence for light snow Friday through Monday night\n  (40%-60%).\n\n- Low confidence Tuesday onward (15%).\n\n- High confidence for wind chills dipping into the low teens to\n  upper single digits (70%-90%).\n\n\nFINDLEY/GAH",
